LESSONS={
'u29-s-active':[
('Distinguish active past and present descriptions','An active participle describes an entity performing the action. The retained чита́вшая is the past reading form; чита́ющая is the present reading form. The labels in the past and in the present distinguish these supplied forms. They do not identify a passive entity being read. An English description of reading can express the action without itself specifying this past/present contrast.'),
('Read the question as well as the form','For чита́ющая, select in the present when asked for its time label. For чита́вшая, select in the past for its own time label. One retained contrast check instead asks for the other time: there the answer is in the present. That reversed question does not turn the displayed past form into a present form. The gloss that read names an action; it is not the requested contrasting time label.'),
('Recognize the separate living example','The retained живу́щие has the meaning living and illustrates an active description. This is recognition of the admitted example, not a general algorithm for generating participles of unfamiliar verbs. Interpreting an isolated form does not establish the complete tense or actor of a sentence that has not been supplied.')],
'u29-s-short-adjective':[
('Recognize the long and short forms','The retained но́вый and нов both mean new. The first is the long form and the second is the short form. Their shared meaning distinguishes them from the colour meanings beige and khaki-colored. Choosing the English gloss alone does not demonstrate selecting the appropriate adjective form in a complete sentence.'),
('Distinguish a predicate from a noun description','A short adjective often supplies the predicate describing its subject; a long adjective often describes a noun attributively. The choice depends on the sentence, not a universal rule about one fixed word position. The retained isolated pair does not provide a complete context for deciding every long-versus-short choice. Do not treat the common predicate/attribute contrast as an exceptionless rule.'),
('A short-looking word need not be a short adjective','The retained беж means beige and is an invariant colour form. Its short appearance does not make it the short counterpart of но́вый. Keep meaning, inflection and adjective function separate. This set checks supplied gloss recognition and explains the contrast; it does not demonstrate productive adjective agreement or sentence-level form selection.')],
'u29-s-bookish-note':[
('Compare two ways of expressing the same sequence','The supplied Пообедав, я пошёл гулять means Having eaten, I went for a walk. The opening verbal adverb presents eating before the walking action. The supplied Я пообедал и пошёл гулять gives the sequence with finite verbs joined together. Both describe the same person eating and then going for a walk; they differ in expression.'),
('Separate register labels from event meaning','In this retained source comparison the verbal-adverb version is labelled bookish speech and the finite-verb version colloquial language. Those labels describe the contrasted register; Having eaten, I went for a walk is the event meaning rather than a register label. A sentence appearing on paper is not automatically bookish, and this pair does not license labelling every verbal adverb in every context as bookish.')],
'u29-s-punctuation':[
('A following descriptive phrase is set off on both sides','In Программа, написанная в спешке, выполнила недопустимую операцию. The phrase describing the program follows its noun and is set off by commas on both sides. The retained label выделяется запятыми с двух сторон names that treatment. A single comma before the phrase would omit its closing boundary in this supplied sentence.'),
('Compare the phrase placed before its noun','In Написанная в спешке программа выполнила недопустимую операцию. The same descriptive phrase precedes the noun. The supplied example has no separating commas: запятые не ставятся is its label. Phrase position helps distinguish these two examples; this does not mean commas are never used before a described noun.'),
('Keep the stated exceptions to the preceding-phrase rule','The retained rule identifies exceptions when the described entity is a personal pronoun or the participial phrase expresses a cause. The displayed личным местоимением names the personal-pronoun case; кроме тех случаев indicates the exception boundary, not the default no-comma treatment. Recognize that exception label here; this small set does not demonstrate punctuation of every unfamiliar participial sentence.')],
'u29-s-gap-register':[
('Contrast the adverbial opening with finite coordination','In Закончив письмо, Анна пошла на почту., finishing the letter is expressed by the opening verbal adverb. In Анна закончила письмо и пошла на почту., the actions are expressed by coordinated finite verbs. The adverbial opening is the bookish option and the finite coordination the ordinary option in this admitted pair. Both describe finishing before going to the post office; the register choice does not reverse those events.'),
('Keep the register claim inside this particular pair','The supplied Написанное письмо лежит на столе. contains a passive description and is outside this adverbial-versus-finite pair. Mere appearance in writing also does not establish this bookish classification. A verbal adverb in a different sentence needs its own contextual evidence: this pair does not license every adverbial as bookish. Recognizing the opening word is different from interpreting the whole sentence or judging an unfamiliar style.')],
'u29-s-gap-reading':[
('Follow the actor and the order of actions','In Закончив письмо, Анна пошла на почту и отправила его., Anna finishes the letter before going to the post office and sending it. Anna performs the actions; the letter does not travel alone and the post office does not write it. The finishing phrase belongs before the departure, not after the sending. Read the entire supplied passage when a check shows only a fragment.'),
('Resolve the final action without substituting a register answer','The supplied отправила его means she sent it, with the letter as the object in this passage. The passage places the sending after Anna goes to the post office. It does not say that she stayed at the table, finished at the market, left the letter at home or received a letter at home. Those alternatives replace a stated event or location. Bookish register classification is a separate objective and cannot answer who acted, where she went or what she did with the letter.')]
}
def digest(s):return hashlib.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()
def repair(p):
 if any(r['itemId'].startswith(PREFIX) for r in p['provenanceRecords']):return p,None
 u=next(u for u in p['units'] if u['number']==29);template=next(r for r in p['provenanceRecords'] if r['itemId']=='prov-ca-17-72');added=[]
 for sid,cards in LESSONS.items():
  s=next(s for s in u['sessions'] if s['id']==sid);obj=s['objectiveIds'][0];ts=[t for t in s['steps'] if t['kind']=='TEACH'];assert len(ts)==len(cards)
  for t,(title,body) in zip(ts,cards):t.update(title=title,body=body)
  s['steps']=ts+[t for t in s['steps'] if t['kind']!='TEACH'];rem=next(t for t in s['steps'] if t['kind']=='REMEDIATE');rem.update(title='Review the complete retained-example contrast',body='\n\n'.join(b for _,b in cards),exampleIds=list(dict.fromkeys(e for t in ts for e in t.get('exampleIds',[]))))
  for t in s['steps']:
   if t['kind'] in ['GUIDED','CHECK']:t['body']='Use the explanation and supplied examples. A missed choice restores every teaching card and worked example.'
  for n,text in enumerate(dict.fromkeys(v for t in s['steps'] for v in [t['title'],t['body']])):
   r=deepcopy(template);original=BIB+'\n'+text;label=sid+'-'+str(n);r.update(itemId=PREFIX+label,unitNumber=29,objectiveId=obj,sourceRecordId='ca-coverage:'+obj+':'+label,originalSourceText=original,shippedText=text,sourceHash=digest(original),contentHash=digest(text),attribution='Russian Companion independently authored English explanation, 2026-10-12; retained examples; no book prose.');r['synthesis'].update(bibliography=BIB,authorshipDeclaration='Independent English instruction, 2026-10-12. No new Russian or copied book expression.',objectiveOrClaimBinding=obj+':'+label);r['synthesis'].pop('applications',None);p['provenanceRecords'].append(r);added.append(r['itemId'])
 return p,added
if __name__=='__main__':
 before=PACK.read_bytes();p,added=repair(loads(before))
 if added:
  after=dumps(p).encode();PACK.write_bytes(after);ledger=dict(previousHead=subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],text=True).strip(),disposition='IMPLEMENTED_PENDING_FINAL_AUDIT',bibliography=BIB,addedProvenanceIds=added,beforeSha256=hashlib.sha256(before).hexdigest(),afterSha256=hashlib.sha256(after).hexdigest());(ROOT/'audit/content-corrections/UNIT29_INSTRUCTION_CORRECTION.json').write_text(json.dumps(ledger,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n');print(len(added),'pending records')
